When I first started playing nethack with the artifacts,
I was playing a wizard and came across an axe called
cleaver.  Ever since I picked it up, my god would get
pissed off at me  (turned out the prayer time-outs had been
changed from the 300 turns it used to be...) but I was conviced
it was because I was wielding Cleaver when I prayed.

Personally, I want the option of using  stormbringer if my
wizard finds it lying around, and I'll accept my god being
angry about it.  Perhaps weilding a non-aligned blade should
make one's god angry ala hitting a friendly creature, like Fluffy.

I would think wielding Stormy would make it easier for me to
change alignment. much easier.

Excalibur is wonderful, in that you don't need to mess with gods
to get it.  I would like to see it as the neutral "most powerful
sword", and let anyone use it.  This obviously can't happen,
because Excalibur is, according to the legends, lawful.

(I've found that saying lawful/chaotic instead of good/evil
keeps the religous fanatics from saying you're pretending to
be an agent of the Devil.  It's worth the inconvenience, just for
the public relations value).

But it's a shame that _the_ one sword that is available to everyone
regardless of alignment is aligned to lawful good.

Perhaps we can get some new weapon from dipping a sword into a
sink's toxic waste?

